      <activity id="0b5d38b0-4e63-50ec-8fb2-95bf87133262" activityNameId="cee2726e-41a6-5ed2-bc19-92f38f0bfec4" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Bark chips, softwood, u=140%, holzpur, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Bark chips, softwood, u=140%, holzpur, at plant
The volume refers to the wood not including the bark. The economic allocation of the process to the three coproducts sawn timber, industrial residue wood and bark chips is done according to specific data on the volume shares and prices of the products. Data on the energy use are specific for the Lang-Sägewerk AG, which delivers the sawn timber to Walter Küng AG for the production of holzpur elements.;
UUID: 9ca68c88-b390-3b0b-8992-1bc20f381470
Includes transport from the forest, debarking and sawing of roundwood at the sawmill.
Location: Data apply to the Lang-Sägewerk in Switzerland.
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at the Lang-Sägewerk AG in Hochdorf-Ligschwil (Switzerland). 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_9ca68c88-b390-3b0b-8992-1bc20f381470.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
